Content licence
================

This covers the editorial content under `content/` — the claims, bodies,
viewpoints, principles and cruxes that Steelview writes. It does not cover
the code, which is MIT-licensed; see the `LICENSE` file at the repository
root.

Steelview's own writing
------------------------

The text Steelview itself writes — every fact's claim and body, every
viewpoint's argument, every principle and every crux — is licensed under

    Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)

Deed:       https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
Legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

You may copy, redistribute, remix, and build on this material for any
purpose, including commercially, as long as you give attribution.

**Attribution.** Because Steelview's editorial policy is deliberately
bylineless — no individual writer is credited for a viewpoint, so that every
side can be held to the same standard — attribution is to the project, not
to a person. Credit it as:

    Steelview (https://steelview.vercel.app/topics/<topic-slug>)

substituting the slug of the topic you are reusing, e.g. for the UK
immigration topic:

    Steelview (https://steelview.vercel.app/topics/uk-immigration)

What this licence does NOT cover
---------------------------------

**The quoted source material is not Steelview's to license.** Every fact on
this site is built on verbatim quotes from third parties — the Office for
National Statistics, the Home Office, the Migration Advisory Committee, the
National Audit Office, the Migration Observatory, Ipsos, and others. Those
quotes are reproduced under quotation for the purpose of letting a reader
check a claim against its source; they are not Steelview's work, and CC BY
4.0 above applies only to Steelview's own surrounding text, not to the
quotations embedded in it.

Each quote carries its own terms, set by its own publisher, and those terms
vary: UK government statistical material (ONS, Home Office, NAO) is
generally published under the Open Government Licence, but other cited
sources — the Migration Advisory Committee, the Migration Observatory,
Ipsos, and any source added to a future topic — set their own terms, which
may differ. **Do not assume a quote is available under CC BY 4.0, or under
the Open Government Licence, or under any single licence.** Every source
record on this site (`stance`, `quote`, `title`, `url`, `publisher`, `date`)
names exactly where the quote came from — check the terms posted at that
`url` before reusing the quoted material itself.

In short: reproduce Steelview's own claims, bodies, viewpoints, principles
and cruxes under CC BY 4.0 with attribution to the project as above; for any
quoted figure or sentence inside them, follow the link to the source and
respect that source's own licence.
